From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Oct 2026 10:55:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: sunxi: pck600: keep the A523 VI/VO0/VO1 domains on

On the A523 nothing in the device tree claims the VI, VO0 and VO1 power
domains: the only in-tree consumers of pck-600 are the display engine and
mixer (PD_DE) and GMAC1 (PD_VO1, disabled on most boards). The TCONs, the
TCON-TOP and the DSI host carry no power-domains property at all.

That is benign until the provider's sync_state() runs. of_genpd_sync_state()
clears ->stay_on on every domain of the provider and tries to power each one
off, so the moment the last deferred consumer probes, every unclaimed domain
is switched off in one sweep - including the ones the display output blocks
live in. Their registers then read back as zero and writes to them are lost,
which looks exactly like a block that is clocked and out of reset but never
configured.

On the Trimui Smart Pro S this also takes down a 5V rail feeding the side
board, killing the LED ring, the gamepad MCUs and the fan until the next
cold boot, because the bootloader is what turns those domains back on.

The vendor device tree marks exactly these three domains "ppu-always-on".
Do the same here with GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON, which this driver already
supports per domain (the A733 table uses it for GPU_CORE).

Tested on a Trimui Smart Pro S (A523) running v7.3-rc7: before the change,
loading sun8i-mixer dropped VE/GPU/VI/VO0/VO1/NAND/PCIE together and the
side board went dark permanently; after it, VI/VO0/VO1 stay on and the
board survives the mixer probe.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5 [Claude Code]
Signed-off-by: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
@@ -202,8 +202,17 @@ err_remove_pds:
 	return ret;
 }

+/*
+ * The vendor device tree marks the VI, VO0 and VO1 domains "ppu-always-on".
+ * Powering them down takes parts of the board down with them, and nothing
+ * claims them from DT, so they would otherwise be switched off as unused as
+ * soon as the provider's sync_state() runs.
+ */
 static const struct sunxi_pck600_pd_desc sun55i_a523_pck600_pds[] = {
-	{ "VE", }, { "GPU", }, { "VI", }, { "VO0", }, { "VO1", },
+	{ "VE", }, { "GPU", },
+	{ "VI", GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON },
+	{ "VO0", GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON },
+	{ "VO1", GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON },
 	{ "DE", }, { "NAND", }, { "PCIE", },
 };

